  "notes": "## Changes since `v0.5.4-beta.3`\n\n### Fixes\n\n- show Codex's work and announce its turns again now that it runs sessions in a shared background server, whose hooks have no terminal to find: the hook then writes the report with the session's id to every terminal running Codex, and the tab Enter was typed in shortly before keeps the session while the others ignore it ([8418e504](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/8418e504a3fb2eadfa55b1fddcd1ee4e1761bcbd))\n- free the GPU buffers of a hidden or closed terminal's WebGL renderer by showing its canvas at one pixel out of sight for a frame before losing the context, since WebKit skips resizing a lost context and keeps the last shown buffer until a later frame, so each released terminal held 100 to 150 MB until a garbage collection that could take hours ([3afae5da](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/3afae5da5290559c398ffc0905faf39d48270761))\n\n**Full comparison:** [v0.5.4-beta.3...v0.5.4-beta.4](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/compare/v0.5.4-beta.3...v0.5.4-beta.4)",
